id: pm-screen-buon
title: Refuse sparse arrays longer than the traversal budget before schema validation
description: "guardSubmitted bounded visited entries but not array length, so a sparse new Array(2 ** 31) passed the guard and schema validation would iterate every empty slot before the schema's max check. Same class CodeRabbit raised on pm-reduce (fixed there in bf3dff0); pm-case and pm-glossary already bound array length."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: dos,input-guard,privacy
created_at: "2026-11-09T12:57:46.112Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T15:05:09.655Z"
assignee: "harness:claude-code"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: Arrays longer than 32768 are refused with invalid_input before validation; a regression covers 2^31 and 32769 (refused) and 64 (allowed) and fails on revert.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T12:57:56.384Z","harness:claude-code","Revert proof: the new test 'guardSubmitted refuses sparse arrays whose length exceeds the traversal budget' fails without the bound and passes with it; test/edge.test.ts passes in full."
  "2026-11-09T15:05:09.653Z","harness:claude-code","Correction after CodeRabbit PRRT_kwDOVll0Ws61TTim and a full-suite run: the per-array cap of 32768 from e345c7a broke the existing contract test 'aggregate node scanning bounds shared graphs and primitive arrays', which allows a dense array of 262143 entries (only the edge file had been run). Many sparse arrays below that cap (127 x 32768 holes) also still passed. The guard now charges each array's holes (length minus present entries; present entries are charged when visited) to the existing 262144 aggregate node budget, with no per-array cap. Full suite 82/82; the holes regression fails against main's guard and passes restored."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  src/privacy.ts,project
  test/edge.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node --test test/edge.test.ts,project,"harness:claude-code","2026-11-09T12:57:51.480Z",local_mutation,fix/bound-sparse-array-length
body: ""
